 475	/// Every content table the flip renders from an artifact, by its header's
 476	/// leading columns. Blind pass 1 at e09ae5e (A09): the gate checked headers,
 477	/// the packet digest, the status tuple, the canary table and the review
 478	/// blocks, and nothing else — so a human-facing cell in any of these could
 479	/// claim a result no artifact supports while every checked thing stayed valid.
 480	/// The activation values the review markdown's test table may use. The packet
 481	/// carries no activation field, so this column is editorial and its vocabulary
 482	/// is closed (A09).
 483	/// Words the flip writes only when an artifact says so. Matched against the
 484	/// WHOLE cell, never as a substring, so a descriptive cell that happens to
 485	/// contain "executed" is not a claim; the tables these guard hold identifiers
 486	/// and results, not prose. While the packet is unqualified no cell anywhere in
 487	/// the review markdown may BE one of them —
 488	/// the content tables are checked cell by cell above, and this catches the
 489	/// `Field | Value` blocks the flip also fills (A09).
 490	/// Words that claim a result. Blind pass 1 at `0a0b4b4b` (A09): `approved`,
 491	/// `accepted`, `granted` and `signed` all assert a decision the flip has not
 492	/// made, and none of them were here — an unqualified packet's report could
 493	/// have said its ratification was approved.
 494	const VERDICT_VOCABULARY: [&str; 16] = [
 495	    "pass",
 496	    "passed",
 497	    "fail",
 498	    "failed",
 499	    "caught",
 500	    "missed",
 501	    "killed",
 502	    "survived",
 503	    "executed",
 504	    "complete",
 505	    "ratified",
 506	    "authorized",
 507	    "approved",
 508	    "accepted",
 509	    "granted",
 510	    "signed",
 511	];
