8206	/// Whether a relative traced path is left out of corpus resolution.
8207	///
8208	/// Relative paths are interpreted against the process cwd or a directory fd,
8209	/// which the trace does not receipt; resolving one as root-relative can hide a
8210	/// locked corpus behind a chdir or alias. A fuzz binary is invoked with an
8211	/// absolute corpus path, so a relative one is the campaign's defect and refuses
8212	/// (`AnyTouch`). A stage's helpers name seeds relative to their cwd (git's
8213	/// index refresh, the campaign's seed manifest) and reviewer tooling opens
8214	/// `../nvidia0` under /dev: unresolvable, and able to add no corpus entry, so
8215	/// under `WritesOnly` every relative path is skipped rather than refused as an
8216	/// escape (F-44). Writes were already judged root-relative by
8217	/// `locked_corpus_write`.
